model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      migrationActivation "Reader-ready migrations use the production release lock and exact live candidate. The trusted main gate loads with Node built-ins before dependency preparation. The activation client is the dispatched main commit: its stack evaluation, readers, pool operator, transport and refusal reports run from main, so a client fix takes effect at merge. The live candidate's prepared checkout supplies only what must match deployed code: the hosted journal SQL and migration CLI, the pool history migrations, its carry and the pool Worker revision. Main's operator refuses when its own migration definitions differ from that candidate's. The client derives the candidate's release identity and a fresh Command attempt before evaluating the stack. A material plan digest binds serving reader versions, signed singleton adoption, installed app versions and exact database preparations. Encrypted pending intent precedes one activation send; an unknown reply blocks ordinary release until inspected. Read-only inspection never creates or resends an activation. Normal preparation never activates, and later releases retain recognized optional cutover markers."
    }
  }
}
